    "explanation": "TO THE RIDER AND TO THE DRIVER — this case goes to a human reviewer. The SGD 4.50 in dispute is held, not collected and not refunded.\n\nWHY. You both agree on the central fact. The chat log records the rider writing 'changed the pin to the other building' at 14:06:43, and the trip record shows the dropoff point was amended 40 seconds later, at 14:07:23 (trip_record.dropoff_amended_at), moving the destination from the original pin 'Blk 7 Everton Park (original pin)' to 'Blk 7 Everton Park'. A dropoff changed after booking means POL-RD-05 applies: the deviation must be re-measured against the route between the AMENDED endpoints, and that route is trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km.\n\nThat figure is not in the record. The amendment timestamp is present but trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km and trip_record.amended_optimal_duration_min are both null. POL-RD-05 says in terms that where this happens the clause cannot be run, the Judge must not derive a substitute figure, and POL-RD-10(5) applies. POL-RD-10(5) names this exact case — an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact that lacks the field the clause requires, including 'a POL-RD-05 amendment with amended_optimal_distance_km null'. POL-RD-10 escalation is TERMINAL: it replaces the ruling, no monetary outcome issues, and the contested amount is frozen. That is why no refund figure appears in this decision.\n\nWHAT IS SETTLED, so the reviewer starts from a clean base:\n- The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02838) is clean for policy purposes: 104 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0. None of the POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment limbs fires, so no independent corroboration is required.\n- Measured against the BOOKED optimal of 10.0 km, the excess is 3.2 km and 32.00% (gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 13.2 km governs over trip_record.actual_distance_km). That clears the POL-RD-01 establishment gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km) but does not reach the materiality gates (over 50% or over 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is triggered and nothing in the driver's profile is used against him: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 207 completed trips, no repeat pattern; prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and is context only under POL-GEN-01. The rider's profile also triggers nothing: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the threshold of 4. Every other profile field on both sides is context only and was not used.\n- The POL-RD-02 arithmetic on the booked baseline is correct but cannot be applied: charged_total 19.32 less recomputed_fare 16.02 (base 3.80 + 0.75 x 10.0 + 0.28 x 14.0, surge 1.0 read from the fare breakdown, plus the 0.80 platform fee) leaves 3.30, above the 0.50 de minimis; that is 17.1% of the charge, so not a full refund. Because 10.0 km is not the correct baseline, 3.30 is illustrative only and is not ordered.\n- No ERP, toll or airport-surcharge money exists on this trip (all such lines are 0.00, erp_gantries is empty), so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity line to refund or refer. POL-RD-06(c) is not triggered either, for the reason above. This ruling therefore carries no referral.\n- POL-RD-04 is unavailable: the rider's chat message carries waypoint_hint null and names no road, so the 200 m corroboration test cannot be run. The pin move is governed by POL-RD-05, not by POL-RD-04 or POL-RD-14, so the argument that the deviation should simply be decided on the trace as measured does not answer the missing re-quote.\n- No circling at the amended point is claimed or shown, so the POL-RD-05 circling exclusion plays no part.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE THIS: the platform's re-quote for the amended dropoff — trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km and trip_record.amended_optimal_duration_min for the route between the booked pickup and the amended dropoff point, or a corrected record showing the amendment did not change the optimal route. With that figure